Operator change: none; this records the decision behind the previous
seven commits. Remove ink specks defaults to 2 px² in Line Art and
Smooth; pixels that touch only at a corner are grouped by one rule in
speck removal, the outline walker (potrace-style minority rule), crack
filling and enlarged-grid support; crack filling closes only grey cracks;
and the speck size keeps a half-pixel margin on enlarged grids.

The record carries the before and after measurements against 85ee406,
including the worse results: Sharp's mean edge error on the thin-lines
image (0.322 to 0.329 px), two more noise outlines in Edge Detection on
the noisy star, twice the CPU time for Smooth on the dragon (4.0 to
8.2 s, from twice the outlines), and five pale marks on the Arch House
logo in Line Art. Sources are potrace's paper, library reference and
manual, Inkscape 1.4.2's trace dialog, and LaserGRBL's vectoriser.

